council of the Society of Incorporated Accountants and Auditors. He was a supporter of the Labour Party, and in 1942 was appointed to London County Council as an alderman. In 1946, he was elected to represent Islington North on the council, and then from 1952 he again served as an alderman. In addition, he served on the Royal Commission on the Press. In April 1953,\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"1787\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"Arthur Middleton died on January 1, 1787. This is a well-documented historical fact regarding the American Founding Father.\"}"
